# EventLinqs line-ending and binary contract.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS, added 3 September 2026. The repository had NO
# .gitattributes at all. With `core.autocrlf = true` on Windows, git checks text
# files out with CRLF, while the test suite writes its proof artefacts with LF.
# Four tracked files therefore came back MODIFIED after every single test run,
# with no change of content whatsoever:
#
#   docs/design/poster-band/hashes.json
#   docs/design/poster-composition/parity.json
#   docs/design/poster-composition/set/INDEX.txt
#   docs/roast/organiser-copy/OUTPUT.md
#
# A permanently dirty tree is not a cosmetic problem. It trains everyone to
# ignore `git status`, and an ignored `git status` is how an unintended change
# eventually rides along inside somebody else's commit.
#
# THE WRITES THEMSELVES ARE ALSO GATED NOW, behind WRITE_PROOF_ARTEFACTS=1, so a
# normal test run does not touch a tracked file in the first place. This file is
# the second half of that fix: it keeps the checked-out bytes and the written
# bytes identical, so the artefacts stay clean even when they ARE regenerated.

# Normalise line endings in the INDEX for everything git detects as text. This
# does not fight autocrlf in the working tree; it stops mixed endings entering
# history.
* text=auto

# The proof artefacts the test suite writes. These are pinned to LF in the
# WORKING TREE, not just the index, because the writer is Node and Node writes
# LF. Anything else reintroduces the phantom diff above.
docs/design/poster-band/hashes.json          text eol=lf
docs/design/poster-composition/parity.json   text eol=lf
docs/design/poster-composition/set/INDEX.txt text eol=lf
docs/roast/organiser-copy/OUTPUT.md          text eol=lf

# Shell scripts and git hooks must keep LF or they will not execute.
*.sh        text eol=lf
.githooks/* text eol=lf

# Binary evidence. Never diffed, never line-ending converted. The poster and
# card PDFs are byte-for-byte deterministic and are compared by hash, so a single
# CRLF substitution inside one would corrupt it and read as a rendering change.
*.pdf   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.avif  binary
*.webp  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.mp4   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
